From 485d4c513ab33b760250fc708d99a2b32a5979ac Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ayiejosh <132535860+ayiejosh@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 23:47:03 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 219/269] gallium/pvr: port the render context's switch
 programs and context state

The firmware never completes this driver's jobs, even a render whose control stream is only
STREAM_TERMINATE. Captured what the working driver sends (temporary env-gated dumps in the Vulkan
tree, reverted after use) and found a whole missing subsystem: the static context state a render
context is created with carries the VDM/GEOM context-state buffers and the PDS store/resume task
programs the firmware switches state with. This driver sent a stream of zeros - a context switch
that saves nothing and restores from address 0.

Now built, following the reference's construction:

- pvr_vm heap bump allocator: programs named by heap-relative offsets (PDS code/data, USC code,
  context-state buffers) are placed at chosen addresses in their heap; one bump pointer per heap.
- context-switch support in pvr_static.c: the precompiled USC SR store/load binaries, their PDS
  launching programs (DOUTW to the USC shared-register buffer + DOUTU), the PT persistent-temp
  store/resume PDS programs, and the two 192-byte static-state groups that name them. Two program
  sets, as the reference builds.
- pvr_gpu_context_create() builds the switch state before CREATE_CONTEXT and passes the populated
  static state; the probe checks the buffers, task words and program sizes.

Also aligned HWRT values to the reference capture for 512x512: tpc 2048 bytes (no 4 KiB clamp),
no RTC, no macrotile array, ISP-merge registers zero, region-header stride from the device formula.

Reference captures for future comparison (context state, fw streams, HWRT values) are archived in
open-driver-perf/captures/real-runs/. Verification: probe still exits 0 ALL PASS under the noop
shim; on the real driver jobs are still accepted and the firmware still does not complete them, so
this was necessary but not sufficient - next is firmware-side evidence (fw trace) or submitting
the reference's exact streams verbatim to separate data from plumbing.
